    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate anchored by the elite offensive upside of **Yordan Alvarez** (80.65), whose xwOBA of 0.469 against Rocker makes him our undisputed top option. Joining him as a priority start is **Christian Yelich** (74.32), who benefits from a favorable matchup against Chandler (5.12 xERA). **Yelich** is a vital play today; his combination of leadoff duties and a high likelihood of a stolen base\u2014aided by Chandler\u2019s slow delivery\u2014provides the elite speed component we prioritize to maintain our lead in the standings. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.78) faces a tough matchup against Lodolo, his speed and placement in the #1 spot secure his position as a high-floor producer for our roster.\n\nOur middle-of-the-pack decisions were heavily dictated by pitching matchups and platoon efficiency. **Lars Nootbaar** (60.61) sneaks into the starting lineup thanks to a strong dynamic platoon edge (+11%), though we are closely monitoring the risk profile of **Junior Caminero** (53.60), who remains a marginal start given the difficult matchup against Gilbert. On the bench, **Luke Raley** (44.01) represents our most difficult omission. **Raley** was firmly in the discussion, but a combination of a pitcher-friendly park and lower projected daily efficiency relative to the rest of the utility corps kept him on the pine. Finally, we must remain vigilant regarding the catchers; **Dillon Dingler** (46.91) is tasked with navigating a tough outing against S\u00e1nchez, and while his base projection is solid, the efficiency drop-off against an elite arm like his makes this a situation to watch. We are proceeding without **Hyeseong Kim**, **Colt Keith**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Josh Smith**, **Carson Benge**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, or **Jacob Gonzalez**, ensuring our capped game slots are reserved strictly for the highest-projected efficiency players like **Kyle Schwarber** (57.25) and **Caleb Durbin** (58.31).",
